{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "# W06 — Model Robustness & Data Audit\n\n**Lane:** Structured Content Archetype Clustering\n\nThis notebook extends W01–W05 using the same unsupervised clustering setup. It focuses on reproducible model robustness, grouped holdout behavior, feature integrity, and sensitivity checks. It intentionally does **not** use research-paper findings or a research-claim-audit section."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 1. Method alignment with W01–W05\n\nW01 defined the decision as content-review prioritization. W02 framed the task as **unsupervised clustering** with no target label. W03 established one content item as the unit of analysis and required explicit checks for grain and missingness. W04 supplied a simple rule baseline. W05 selected K-Means with eight core numeric features, median imputation, selective log transforms, and RobustScaler.\n\nThe audit below keeps those choices fixed: the validation question is whether the same feature representation produces reasonably consistent archetypes when the model is fitted on one set of clients and evaluated on unseen clients. This is a robustness check, not a claim that the clusters are ground-truth labels."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import RobustScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import silhouette_score\n",
    "\n",
    "DATA_PATH = \"data/raw/content_refresh_anonymized.csv\"\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(DATA_PATH)\n",
    "\n",
    "core_features = [\n",
    "    \"search_volume\", \"word_count\", \"content_age_days\",\n",
    "    \"days_since_last_update\", \"impressions_90d\", \"ctr\",\n",
    "    \"avg_position\", \"engagement_rate\",\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "required = [\"content_id\", \"client_id\"] + core_features\n",
    "missing_required = [c for c in required if c not in df.columns]\n",
    "print(\"Rows:\", len(df))\n",
    "print(\"Clients:\", df[\"client_id\"].nunique())\n",
    "print(\"Missing required columns:\", missing_required)\n",
    "assert not missing_required\n",
    "assert len(core_features) == 8\n",
    "assert df[\"content_id\"].nunique() == len(df), \"Expected one row per content item\"\n",
    "print(\"\\nW05 feature contract reproduced successfully.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 2. Grouped holdout: unseen-client check\n\nA random row split can place very similar content from the same client in both train and test. Because the project contains multiple clients, a grouped split is a stricter test of whether the feature pattern transfers to unseen clients. The preprocessing objects are fitted on the training clients only. Test rows are assigned to the nearest training centroid."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Deterministic 80/20 client-group split.\n",
    "clients = np.array(sorted(df[\"client_id\"].dropna().unique()))\n",
    "rng = np.random.RandomState(42)\n",
    "rng.shuffle(clients)\n",
    "n_train_clients = max(1, int(len(clients) * 0.80))\n",
    "train_clients = set(clients[:n_train_clients])\n",
    "test_clients = set(clients[n_train_clients:])\n",
    "\n",
    "train_mask = df[\"client_id\"].isin(train_clients)\n",
    "test_mask = df[\"client_id\"].isin(test_clients)\n",
    "\n",
    "train_df = df.loc[train_mask].copy()\n",
    "test_df = df.loc[test_mask].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Train clients:\", len(train_clients))\n",
    "print(\"Test clients:\", len(test_clients))\n",
    "print(\"Train rows:\", len(train_df))\n",
    "print(\"Test rows:\", len(test_df))\n",
    "assert train_clients.isdisjoint(test_clients)\n",
    "assert len(train_df) + len(test_df) == len(df)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Fit preprocessing ONLY on train. This prevents test information entering the representation.\n",
    "X_train_raw = train_df[core_features].copy()\n",
    "X_test_raw = test_df[core_features].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# In W05, avg_position = 0 means no position data, not rank zero.\n",
    "X_train_raw[\"avg_position\"] = X_train_raw[\"avg_position\"].replace(0, np.nan)\n",
    "X_test_raw[\"avg_position\"] = X_test_raw[\"avg_position\"].replace(0, np.nan)\n",
    "\n",
    "imputer = SimpleImputer(strategy=\"median\")\n",
    "X_train = pd.DataFrame(imputer.fit_transform(X_train_raw), columns=core_features, index=train_df.index)\n",
    "X_test = pd.DataFrame(imputer.transform(X_test_raw), columns=core_features, index=test_df.index)\n",
    "\n",
    "log_features = [\"search_volume\", \"word_count\", \"impressions_90d\"]\n",
    "for col in log_features:\n",
    "    X_train[col] = np.log1p(X_train[col].clip(lower=0))\n",
    "    X_test[col] = np.log1p(X_test[col].clip(lower=0))\n",
    "\n",
    "scaler = RobustScaler()\n",
    "X_train_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X_train)\n",
    "X_test_scaled = scaler.transform(X_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "kmeans = KMeans(n_clusters=3, random_state=42, n_init=10)\n",
    "train_labels = kmeans.fit_predict(X_train_scaled)\n",
    "test_labels = kmeans.predict(X_test_scaled)\n",
    "\n",
    "train_silhouette = silhouette_score(X_train_scaled, train_labels)\n",
    "test_silhouette = silhouette_score(X_test_scaled, test_labels)\n",
    "\n",
    "train_pct = pd.Series(train_labels).value_counts(normalize=True).sort_index() * 100\n",
    "test_pct = pd.Series(test_labels).value_counts(normalize=True).sort_index() * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "comparison = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"train_pct\": train_pct.round(2),\n",
    "    \"test_pct\": test_pct.round(2),\n",
    "}).fillna(0)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Train silhouette: {train_silhouette:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Unseen-client test silhouette: {test_silhouette:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Silhouette difference (test - train): {test_silhouette - train_silhouette:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(\"\\nCluster share comparison (%):\")\n",
    "display(comparison)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 3. Feature integrity and leakage checks\n\nThe clustering task has no prediction target. The audit therefore checks that identifiers, future/trend labels, and obvious outcome proxies are not in the eight-feature matrix. It also verifies that imputation and scaling were fitted only on the grouped training set."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "identifier_terms = [\"id\", \"hash\", \"client\"]\n",
    "future_terms = [\"future\", \"trend\", \"decline\", \"label\", \"target\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "identifier_features = [c for c in core_features if any(t in c.lower() for t in identifier_terms)]\n",
    "future_features = [c for c in core_features if any(t in c.lower() for t in future_terms)]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Identifier-like core features:\", identifier_features)\n",
    "print(\"Future/target-like core features:\", future_features)\n",
    "print(\"Core feature count:\", len(core_features))\n",
    "\n",
    "assert identifier_features == []\n",
    "assert future_features == []\n",
    "assert imputer.statistics_.shape[0] == len(core_features)\n",
    "assert scaler.center_.shape[0] == len(core_features)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nPASS — no identifiers or future/target labels are used as clustering features.\")\n",
    "print(\"PASS — preprocessing was fitted on train data and then applied to test data.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Missingness audit before imputation.\n",
    "missing_audit = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"train_missing_pct\": X_train_raw.isna().mean() * 100,\n",
    "    \"test_missing_pct\": X_test_raw.isna().mean() * 100,\n    "}).round(2)\n",
    "\n",
    "display(missing_audit)\n",
    "print(\"Total missing values after train-fitted imputation — train:\", int(np.isnan(X_train_scaled).sum()))\n",
    "print(\"Total missing values after train-fitted imputation — test:\", int(np.isnan(X_test_scaled).sum()))\n",
    "assert not np.isnan(X_train_scaled).any()\n",
    "assert not np.isnan(X_test_scaled).any()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 4. Sensitivity to initialization\n\nW05 already checked multiple random seeds. Repeating the check here gives a compact audit result using the same K=3, eight-feature representation. If silhouette and cluster proportions stay close, the result is less dependent on one K-Means initialization."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "seed_results = []\n",
    "reference = train_labels\n",
    "\n",
    "for seed in [0, 1, 7, 42, 123]:\n",
    "    km = KMeans(n_clusters=3, random_state=seed, n_init=10)\n",
    "    labels = km.fit_predict(X_train_scaled)\n",
    "    sil = silhouette_score(X_train_scaled, labels)\n",
    "    sizes = pd.Series(labels).value_counts(normalize=True).sort_index() * 100\n",
    "    seed_results.append({\n",
    "        \"seed\": seed,\n",
    "        \"silhouette\": round(sil, 4),\n",
    "        \"largest_cluster_pct\": round(sizes.max(), 2),\n",
    "        \"smallest_cluster_pct\": round(sizes.min(), 2),\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "seed_results_df = pd.DataFrame(seed_results)\n",
    "display(seed_results_df)\n",
    "print(f\"Silhouette range: {seed_results_df['silhouette'].min():.4f} - {seed_results_df['silhouette'].max():.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Largest-cluster range: {seed_results_df['largest_cluster_pct'].min():.2f}% - {seed_results_df['largest_cluster_pct'].max():.2f}%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## Final audit summary\n\nThe model is treated as a descriptive grouping mechanism. The strongest evidence from this notebook is whether the eight-feature K-Means representation remains reasonably separated on unseen clients and whether the cluster-size pattern is broadly similar between train and test. A large train/test drop or unstable seed results would be a reason to revisit the feature set, K, or data coverage before using the archetypes for prioritization.\n\nNo research-paper findings, causal claims, or research-claim-audit material are used here."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "checks = {\n",
    "    \"one row per content\": df[\"content_id\"].nunique() == len(df),\n",
    "    \"exactly 8 core features\": len(core_features) == 8,\n",
    "    \"no identifier features\": len(identifier_features) == 0,\n",
    "    \"no future/target features\": len(future_features) == 0,\n",
    "    \"train/test clients disjoint\": train_clients.isdisjoint(test_clients),\n",
    "    \"train preprocessing has no missing values\": not np.isnan(X_train_scaled).any(),\n",
    "    \"test preprocessing has no missing values\": not np.isnan(X_test_scaled).any(),\n",
    "    \"seed sensitivity was measured\": len(seed_results_df) == 5,\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "for name, passed in checks.items():\n",
    "    print((\"PASS\" if passed else \"FAIL\") + \" — \" + name)\n",
    "\n",
    "assert all(checks.values())\n",
    "print(\"\\nAll automated W06 robustness/data-audit checks passed.\")"
   ]
  }
 ],
